<title>USA: FOCUS- Sun union deal not enough -analysts.</title>
<headline>FOCUS- Sun union deal not enough -analysts.</headline>
<byline>Matt Daily</byline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Jan 15 (Reuter) The agreement reached Wednesday between Sun Co Inc and workers at its Marcus Hook refinery will help cut losses but it is not enough to make the unit competitive in the cut-throat U.S. refining business, analysts said.</p>
<p>The $14 million the company expects to save from layoffs &quot;only skims the surface. They will definetly have to go much deeper,&quot; said Fedel Gheit, analyst with Fahnestock &amp; Company.</p>
</text>
